==Galician==
[[File:Pontedeume-Castelo de Andrade 07.jpg|thumb|Castle of Andrade, Pontedeume]]

===Etymology===
From {{inh|gl|LL.|Andreati}} (attested in Dalmatia, 6th century, ''CIL'' III 9561), late genitive form of {{m|la|Andreas||Andrew}}, from {{der|gl|grc|Ἀνδρέας|Ἀνδρέᾱς}}; so meaning "Andrew's" (place/villa/property).

During the Late Middle Ages this became the surname of a powerful noble family from Northern Galicia, later passing into Portugal, Spain, the rest of Europe, the New World and the Philippines.

